<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George William, Duke of Legnica</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1660">1660</a>–<a href="/years/1675">1675</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George William, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legnica">Legnica</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brzeg">Brzeg</a> and Wołów, was the last male member of the Silesian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piasts</a>, the branch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>'s first royal dynasty that had ruled Silesian duchies since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. He came of age and took power in 1675 but died the same year aged fifteen, and his duchies passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> as kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-william-duke-of-legnica.jpg" alt="George William, Duke of Legnica" width="320" height="492" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Tscherning / After Benjamin Block · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_William,_Duke_of_Liegnitz.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
